{"name":"Chocolate Bar","hex":"#773333","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chocolate bar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat, typically rectangular bar of solid chocolate designed to be easily partitioned into smaller squares or segments.","A kind of candy in the shape of a bar, often made of chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chocolate_bar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chocolate bar","blocks":[{"text":"A chocolate bar is a confection containing chocolate, which may also contain layerings or mixtures that include nuts, fruit, caramel, nougat, and wafers. A flat and easily partitionable chocolate bar is also called a tablet. In some varieties of English and food labeling standards, the term chocolate bar is reserved for bars of solid chocolate, with candy bar used for products with additional ingredients."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Green_and_Black%27s_dark_chocolate_bar_2.jpg/330px-Green_and_Black%27s_dark_chocolate_bar_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate_bar"},{"title":"Chocolate","blocks":[{"text":"Chocolate is a food made from roasted and ground cocoa beans. It can be a liquid, solid, or paste. It is eaten on its own and used to flavor other foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg/330px-Three_Bars_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chocolate"},{"title":"Chocolate (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color chocolate or cocoa brown is a shade of brown that resembles chocolate. At right is displayed the color traditionally called chocolate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Chocolate02.jpg/330px-Chocolate02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik